# Stripe Invoices

When the user asks to create or send a Stripe invoice:

1. Use `scripts/create-invoice.js` — reads `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` from project `.env`.
2. Stripe emails the client automatically (`sendInvoice`); no website UI or webhook required.
3. Required: `--email`, `--description`, `--amount` (dollars). Optional: `--name`, `--due` (days, default 30).

Example:

```bash
node scripts/create-invoice.js \
  --email client@example.com \
  --name "Jane Client" \
  --description "Website maintenance — March 2026" \
  --amount 1500 \
  --due 30
```

Do not expose `.env` values. `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` and `INVOICE_API_SECRET` are optional for this workflow.
